
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The arrival of the MacBook Pro PROLED XDR felt, at first, a bit underwhelming to me. But early reviews seem to like it.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jason Snell&#8217;s <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/11/macbook-pro-with-proled-review-you-could-even-say-it-glows/">review at Six Colors</a> gives the reduced weight plenty of attention. He also looks at the OLED display and describes touch as an occasional extra way to interact with the Mac. It&#8217;s a useful look at changes you&#8217;ll notice while carrying and using the thing.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At Tom&#8217;s Guide, Tony Polanco has <a href="https://www.tomsguide.com/computing/macbooks/macbook-pro-with-proled-xdr-display-review">published a full PROLED MacBook Pro review</a>. He&#8217;s enthusiastic about the display and touch controls, with the price as his main reservation. There are battery results, too, and they&#8217;re not bad.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Also, Marques Brownlee has <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2reQut8WNGc">posted his first impressions of the PROLED XDR MacBook Pro</a>.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The screen and weight deserve attention, even if you&#8217;re not interested in the touch display.</p>



